SUMMARY:OpenClawNet - Skills + Memory
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn this session we will personalize
  the agent with skills — reusable knowledge bundles defined in Markdown 
 with YAML frontmatter — and add conversation memory so it retains contex
 t across sessions. We will build a skill loader\, implement automatic summ
 arization to manage token budgets\, and create a UI to toggle skills on an
 d off in real time.\n\nAt the end we will have an agent that adapts its ex
 pertise based on loaded skills and remembers your preferences across conve
 rsations. Add a "Git Expert" skill or a "JavaScript Mentor" skill and watc
 h the agent's behavior change. Your users can create custom skills without
  touching code.\n\n**Key Topics & Technologies:**\n\n* Skill architecture 
 (Markdown + YAML)\n* Markdown parsing and metadata extraction\n* In-memory
  caching and skill composition\n* Conversation memory and summarization st
 rategies\n* Token budgeting and context window management\n* Skill UI with
  toggle controls\n* Workspace customization patterns\n\nPre-requisites:\n\
 n* **Experience:** Intermediate C# and ASP.NET Core knowledge (not a .NET 
 101)\n* **Environment:** .NET 10 SDK\, VS Code + GitHub Copilot (or Visual
  Studio)\, Docker (for Ollama)\n* **Optional:** Azure subscription (for Se
 ssions 3–4\, but local development works fine throughout)\n* **Mindset:*
 * Curiosity about AI agents\, willingness to follow along live and ask que
 stions
