DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn a world of multiple tools and en
 dless data sources\, how do you design the right integration strategy in M
 icrosoft Fabric?\n\nJoin us for a live demo-driven session that breaks dow
 n the real-world patterns\, use cases\, and best practices for landing\, t
 ransforming\, and orchestrating data in Microsoft Fabric.\n\nWhether you'r
 e working with a Lakehouse\, Data Warehouse\, Eventhouse\, or SQL Database
 \, this session gives you the playbook to select and combine the right too
 ls for the job.\n\nWe'll walk through:\n\n* Landing data using Data Pipeli
 nes\, OneLake shortcuts\, and external connections\n* Transforming and cle
 aning data using Notebooks (Spark) for scale and flexibility\n* Business l
 ogic and last-mile transformation using Dataflows Gen2\n* How to orchestra
 te it all using Fabric Data Pipelines for repeatable\, maintainable workfl
